## Completed: lucebox-hub-gfx1151-8lk

**Solution**: Use NVIDIA GV100GL (Tesla PG503-216) with CUDA backend instead of AMD gfx1151 APU with HIP/ROCm.

### What was implemented:
1. Built llama.cpp with CUDA backend (compute capability sm_70)
2. Built dflash with CUDA backend + TriAttention support
3. Solved CUDA 12.5 + GCC 13 incompatibility by using GCC-12 as host compiler

### Performance improvement:
| Metric | gfx1151 APU (HIP) | GV100GL (CUDA) |
|--------|-------------------|----------------|
| Model load (15 GiB) | 3+ hours | ~10 seconds |
| Baseline gen speed | N/A (hangs) | 20.4 tok/s |
| DFlash speed | N/A (hangs) | 17.2 tok/s |

The NVIDIA GV100GL GPU has 32 GB VRAM and runs the Qwen3.6-27B Q4_K_M model successfully with both `test_generate` and `test_dflash` binaries.
